        "id": "dr4040_430-req-012",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "must ensure expectations reflect the respective employee’s actual duties and responsibilities, and are clearly and specifically communicated.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-013",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "3 Generic standards must be commensurate with the grade of the positions to which they are assigned.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-014",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "must: 1 Communicate in writing the elements for the position, and each element’s performance standards and measures; 2 Contain all elements that will be used in deriving and assigning a summary rating; 3 Include: a A minim",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-015",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "This element must also reflect the civil rights-related expectations related to the employee’s program responsibilities.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-016",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "supervisors and managers must contain an element for general supervision and leadership that includes: a Expectations related to performance management; b Expectations related to supervisory civil rights and Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) responsibilities; and c Expectations related to employee engagement.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-017",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "(a) An approved performance plan must be issued to eligible employees no later than: 1 30 days from the beginning of the new performance year; 2 15 days from when an employee starts a new position, a detail, or temporary promotion of 90 or more days; or 3 15 days from a new a",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-018",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "plans for subordinate employees must be reviewed with the employees within 30 days, and revised as necessary, consistent with Sections 5f(5) and (6).",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-019",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "(a) Rating Officials must formally communicate expectations before holding employees accountable for them.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-020",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
