        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-021",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "Performance plans are not required to be uniform, but they must be fair and equitable throughout a Reviewing Official’s respective organizations.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-022",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "(a) Rating Officials must have a specific conversation with each employee to discuss performance no less than once each quarter.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-023",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "(i) Rating Officials must initial and date, and ask their employees to initial and date, the Form AD-435E, Form AD-435S, or approved electronic alternative to document the reviews have taken place.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-024",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "(a) Employee plans must be updated during the performance year when minor changes need to be documented, for example: 1 Clarification of standards and measures; 2 New organizational goals or priorities that do not significantly impact the original standards; or 3",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-025",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "2 Rating Officials must document and keep records of all such modifications and related conversations to demonstrate the employee was informed; and 3 If these changes are made in an electronic system, they may be noted in a comments section.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-026",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "(a) Employee plans must be revised during the performance year when significant changes need to be documented, for example: 1 Adding a substantial new expectation; or 14 2 Adding a significant new standard or measure.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-027",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "Rating and Reviewing Officials must complete ratings of record as soon as practicable after the end of the appraisal period, and issue them to employees no later than October 30th.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-028",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "1 A rating of record must be produced: a Following the end of the performance year, provided the employee has performed under an established plan for a minimum of 90 days, which need not be consecutive; b When a within-grade increase (WGI) decision is not consistent with",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-029",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "3 Ratings must be based on actual employee performance during the performance year.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-030",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "b Ratings of record must not be carried forward from a previous appraisal period.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-031",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "a Each performance element must be evaluated separately, based on actual performance, accomplishments, contributions, and results.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-032",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "Fully Successful level of an element’s standards and measures must be entirely met before assigning that element rating.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-033",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "determination must be specifically documented in a narrative assessment for the element.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-034",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "e The Rating Official must prepare a narrative assessment supporting the proposed evaluation of any element below the Fully Successful level. The narrative must: 18 i. Specify the factual details regarding any expectations not met r",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-035",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "The narrative must: 18 i. Specify the factual details regarding any expectations not met relative to each element that is evaluated at the Does Not Meet Fully Successful level; and ii. Be based on documentary or other",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-036",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "a The Rating Official must provide the proposed ratings and any required narrative assessment to the Reviewing Official for consideration.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-037",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
