        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-053",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "2 Interim ratings must specify the date range of the performance.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-054",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "3 Interim ratings must be completed within 15 days of the conclusion of the abbreviated appraisal period, including issuing the rating to the employee and providing a copy to the Rating Official who will be assessing the employee’s performance at the end of the performance year.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-055",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "performance year, in consultation with the Reviewing Official, must consider the nature of assignments and the length of time covered by the interim rating(s) when determining the impact of the interim rating(s) on the employee’s element and summary ratings that comprise the rating of record.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-056",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "(2) The Rating Official must evaluate the employee’s performance against each element in the performance plan, and, because in some situations an interim rating may become the rating of record, propose a summary interim rating to the Reviewing Official.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-057",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "assessment must be produced within 15 days of the end of the temporary assignment or of the effective date of the revised plan.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-058",
        "section": "5",
        "section_title": "Performance Management",
        "text": "(b) The supervisor of the abbreviated performance period must document: 1 The primary expectations during the abbreviated performance period (if not already described in a performance plan); 2 Whether the employee met the expectations; and 3 The date range of the performance.",
        "keyword": "must",
        "mandatory": true,
    },
    {
        "id": "dr4040_430-req-059",
        "section": "5",
